Z||000000||Richard Parnell||10-06-2000||02:22 PM||||I'm in the midst of a V8 conversion on my 87 SC.  My buddy who is actaully doing most of the work since he is in the business and has done 4 other Fiero V8 conversions, wants to get rid of the electric fuel pump in the gas tank and use a regular fuel pump mounted at the normal spot on the engine.  He did this on his own Fiero w/350 after the stock Fiero pump burned out 4 times on his car.  This happened even with a regulator in the line.  I'm inclined to go along with him since there seems to be room for the chevy fuel pump to clear everything when the motor is installed.  Does anyone have any feed back and/or experience with this?  Archie, Ogre?||||reg||1
